   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public health law, in relation to prohibiting the advertisement of tobacco products and herbal cigarettes near schools",
    "basePrintNo": "S4522",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4522-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add Art 13-I §§1399-aaa - 1399-ccc, Pub Health L",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S4522\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the public health law, in relation to prohibiting the\nadvertisement of tobacco products and herbal cigarettes near schools\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nTo amend the public health law to prohibit the advertisement of\ntobacco products within 1,000 feet of a school.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nThis bill would amend the public health law by prohibiting the\nadvertising, marketing or promotion of tobacco products within 1,000\nfeet of school grounds and establishing civil penalties of $250 to\n$1,000 for a first violation, $500 to $2,000 for a second violation\nand a minimum of $1,000 for each subsequent violation.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\n\nExisting state law establishes a toll-free telephone hotline to\nprovide information regarding health care providers and treatment\ncenters with expertise in illnesses associated with military duty.\nThere is also a federal veterans' crisis line.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nA great portion of tobacco advertisement and promotion is designed to\nattract the attention of our youth. By prohibiting tobacco\nadvertisements in and around our schools, we can better protect our\nstate's young people from marketing efforts which are designed to get\nthem to try tobacco products.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\n01/22/16 Referred to Health\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone\n\n LOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect on the first of September next succeeding\nthe date on which it shall have become a law.\n",
