    "lawCode": "Add Art 13-I §§1399-aaa - 1399-ccc, Pub Health L",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4522A\n\nSPONSOR: SANDERS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public health law, in relation to prohibiting the\nadvertisement of tobacco products and herbal cigarettes near schools\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo amend the public health law to prohibit the advertisement of tobacco\nproducts within 500 feet of a school.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill would amend the public health law by prohibiting the advertis-\ning, marketing or promotion of tobacco products within 500 feet of\nschool grounds and establishing civil penalties of $250 to $1,000 for a\nfirst violation, $500 to $2,000 for a second violation and a minimum of\n$1,000 for each subsequent violation.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nExisting state law establishes a toll-free telephone hotline to provide\ninformation regarding health care providers and treatment centers with\nexpertise in illnesses associated with military duty.  There is also a\nfederal veterans' crisis line.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nA great portion of tobacco advertisement and promotion is designed to\nattract the attention of our youth. By prohibiting tobacco advertise-\nments in and around our schools, we can better protect our state's young\npeople from marketing efforts which are designed to get them to try\ntobacco products.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n01/22/16 Referred to Health\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the first of September next succeeding the\ndate on which it shall have become a law.\n",
